# DEPRECATED — do not proxy rosbridge through nginx.
#
# This file used to hold one `location /robot/<name>` block per robot, proxying
# straight to the robot's rosbridge (:9090). rosbridge has no authentication,
# so that let anyone who could load the page drive the robot whatever their
# role, or with no account at all.
#
# Browsers now reach robots only through the backend, at
# /backend/api/robots/<id>/ros: it checks the session, refuses what the
# person's role does not allow, records commands in the audit trail, and relays
# the rest to the robot's registered bridge_url. Nothing needs configuring here
# for that; the /backend/ location already carries the WebSocket.
#
# What to do instead:
#   1. Delete any /robot/<name> block from /opt/amr/nginx/robots.conf (or the
#      whole file), then `docker compose restart web`.
#   2. In the registry, set each robot's bridge URL to its direct address,
#      ws://<jetson-ip>:9090. Only the backend uses it.
#   3. Firewall rosbridge on each robot so only the server can reach it, e.g.
#        sudo ufw allow from <server-ip> to any port 9090 proto tcp
#        sudo ufw deny 9090/tcp
#
# This file may still hold other per-site nginx extras; it is included inside
# the server block of the web container.
